WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070
Pick up an ordinary battery.

2
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.290
Printed on the side: 1.5 volts.

3
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.810
Look at a small lamp.

4
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.540
Stamped on its base: 6 volts.

5
00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.110
We read volts on chargers, batteries
and power supplies every day.

6
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.720
But a volt has to be a count of something.

7
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.750
So what exactly does one volt count?

8
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.810
In this mission, you'll follow
charge around a circuit,

9
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.520
and pin down what a voltmeter
measures between two points.

10
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.260
Then you'll watch 3 coulombs
pass through that 6 volt lamp,

11
00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.990
and see what it gives out.

12
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.260
Your mission: find out
exactly what a volt counts,

13
00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.470
then use it in a calculation.
